# Max agents (owner-set 2026-08-14)

Always fill every independent workflow with its own agent. Goal: about **3×** wall-clock vs one serial session.

- **Max out.** Do not sit at one agent when a second could work. Launch the full set in one turn.
- **Spread.** One agent per screen, module, or file fence. Never two writers on the same file.
- **No fake parallel.** If B needs A’s output, B waits. Everything else runs now.
- **Grok only** (see grok-only-agents). Design stays Claude rule — still its own session, not a Grok stand-in.
- Shared board in `docs/workflows/`. Claim before write. Cap is “all independent units,” not 5.
